{"additions":1037,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Summary\n\nThe Projects page now shows the GitHub Projects (v2) **linked to the current repository** (`gh repo view --json projectsV2`) instead of listing every project of the owner, and the board takes the full width by default — the first linked board appears immediately on `7`. Implements #128 (page design: #119).\n\n## Changes\n\n- **Scope**: data source is `gh repo view --json nameWithOwner,owner,projectsV2`; the owner-wide `gh project list` and the GraphQL `updatedAt` query are removed. The project owner (`--owner` for `gh project field-list` / `item-list`) is derived from each node's `resourcePath` (`/users/...` or `/orgs/...`).\n- **Default layout**: builtin `page \"projects\"` places only `board` (top, full width) and `detail`; `tabs \"board\" \"detail\"`. The `projects` list pane stays implemented but **unplaced**; the builtin `bind select=\"projects\" detail=\"board\"` is kept and applies as soon as a user layout places the pane (example in `docs/config.md`).\n- **Selection among linked projects**: one link → its board loads on activation; several → the header shows `Board: <title> (i/n)` and `p` / `P` (view actions `NextProject` / `PrevProject`) cycle and reload; none → the board pane shows \"No projects are linked to this repository (link one from the repository's Projects tab or `gh project link`)\".\n- **Loader**: a `pane` block may stay unplaced (inactive pane): pane IDs come from the pane blocks in declaration order, a layout may place each pane **at most once** (placing twice, or nothing, is an error), unplaced panes are skipped by `tabs` cycling and focus, and `bind` entries naming an unplaced pane are ignored.\n- **Cross-repo cards**: a card whose item lives in another repository shows a dimmed `owner/repo` prefix before `#n`.\n- Detail (Fields), table mode, sort, search, `o`, the disk cache (boards keyed by project number; a pre-change owner-wide `list.json` is ignored) and the scope-error notice are kept.\n- **Docs**: README / README.ja Projects sections, `docs/config.md` (unplaced-pane rules, projects page example), CLAUDE.md checklist (\"every pane placed exactly once\" → \"at most once; unplaced panes are inactive\").\n- **Demo**: `tape/demo-projects.tape` re-recorded — `7` shows the board immediately (no more project-list step or `gh` PATH shim), then column moves, table mode, detail.\n\n## Not verified\n\n- A repository whose linked project belongs to an **organization** (`/orgs/...` `resourcePath`) — covered by unit tests, not exercised against a live org project.\n- The zero-linked-projects notice and `p` / `P` cycling with several linked projects are covered by unit tests only; the demo repository has exactly one linked project.\n- Very old `gh` versions that omit `projectsV2` from `gh repo view --json` (parsed as \"no links\").\n\nCloses #128\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TreGn5Xh4PjDRv9Yo4QU4w","changedFiles":17,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-08-31T02:43:59Z","deletions":550,"headRefName":"feat/projects-linked-only","labels":[],"number":129,"reviewDecision":"","reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLcOfsQ","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThe new “unplaced panes are allowed” loader behavior can leave other pages’ initial focus pointing at an inactive pane (breaking focus/navigation) unless focus normalization is added when constructing/activating pages.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull request overview</summary>\n\nThis PR updates the Projects page to scope its data source to GitHub Projects (v2) **linked to the current repository** (via `gh repo view --json ... projectsV2`) and changes the default Projects layout so the board is **full width** and loads immediately, while still keeping the optional projects list pane available for user layouts. It also extends the config loader to allow panes to be defined-but-unplaced (inactive) and adds new view actions (`p` / `P`) to cycle among multiple linked projects.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Projects page now reads linked projects from `gh repo view` and cycles among them with `p` / `P`; board loads immediately and supports cross-repo card prefixes.\n- Default `projects` page layout places only `board` + `detail` (full width board), leaving the `projects` list pane unplaced/inactive by default.\n- Config loader now permits unplaced panes (inactive), filters `tabs`/`bind` behavior accordingly, and validates “placed at most once”.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>File summaries</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| tape/demo-projects.tape | Updates the demo flow to show Projects board immediately without the previous `gh` shim step. |\r\n| src/projects/state.rs | Switches Projects state to repo-linked projects, adds project cycling (`p`/`P`), notices, and focus behavior when list pane is unplaced. |\r\n| src/projects/panes/projects.rs | Updates list pane semantics for linked projects only; supports board-driven item counts and revised row rendering. |\r\n| src/projects/panes/board.rs | Adds cross-repo card prefixing, supports optional list-pane back navigation, and introduces board notices. |\r\n| src/projects/domain/types.rs | Introduces `RepoInfo` linked-project parsing from `gh repo view` and derives project owners from `resourcePath`. |\r\n| src/projects/domain/disk_cache.rs | Ignores legacy (pre-repo-scoped) cached project lists and caches linked project lists. |\r\n| src/projects/domain/client.rs | Simplifies client to rely on `gh repo view` + `gh project field-list/item-list` only. |\r\n| src/core/ui/status_bar.rs | Enhances Projects header with current board title and `(i/n)` indicator; adjusts status wording to “linked projects”. |\r\n| src/core/keymap.rs | Adds `ViewAction::NextProject` / `PrevProject` and help text. |\r\n| src/core/config/loader.rs | Allows panes to be unplaced (inactive), tracks `placed_ids`, filters binds/tabs for inactive panes, and enforces “at most once” placement. |\r\n| README.md | Updates Projects documentation to reflect linked-project scope, full-width board, `p`/`P` cycling, and optional list pane. |\r\n| docs/README.ja.md | Japanese docs update mirroring the new Projects behavior and keybindings. |\r\n| docs/config.md | Documents new loader rules: unplaced panes are inactive; tabs/binds skip/ignore them; layout must place at least one pane. |\r\n| CLAUDE.md | Updates architectural/docs checklist notes to match the new unplaced-pane behavior and Projects changes. |\r\n| assets/demo-projects.gif | Re-recorded demo GIF (LFS pointer updated). |\r\n| assets/default.kdl | Changes built-in Projects layout to board+detail only; adds `p`/`P` view bindings; documents optional list-pane layout snippet. |\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 16/16 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 1\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/td72/vig/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review?tool=webui#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T02:48:38Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"bf82174d5cafd3442b42824aa89d0c0e8649c67f"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLcdzRA","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T04:01:38Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"bf82174d5cafd3442b42824aa89d0c0e8649c67f"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLcg-pw","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T04:16:21Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"7efb65a269fdf315f928905d423ccc99ea819ccb"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLchjIg","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nBoard caching/inflight tracking is keyed only by project number (not owner/id), which can collide for linked projects from different owners, and focus fallback can still leave focus on an unrendered pane when `tab_panes` is empty.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 17/17 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 2\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T04:18:43Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"7efb65a269fdf315f928905d423ccc99ea819ccb"}}],"state":"MERGED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T04:22:44Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33356870583/job/99380615327","name":"create-tag","startedAt":"2026-08-31T04:22:44Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T04:17:16Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33356470255/job/99379499980","name":"build (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-31T04:15:57Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T04:16:27Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33356470207/job/99379